title: Brand Identity & Guidelines
description: Naked Tech Brand v2 guidelines covering positioning, voice, visual identity, light and dark themes, components and customer experience.
---

<div class="bg-canvas min-h-screen pt-32 pb-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-6xl">

        <!-- Hero / Introduction -->
        <div class="mb-16 md:mb-24">
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-4 text-accent-ink">Internal Documentation — Brand v2 · July 2026</p>
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold text-ink mb-6 tracking-tight">
                Brand Identity &amp; Guidelines
            </h1>
            <p class="text-lg max-w-3xl text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
                Naked Tech combines <strong class="text-ink">transparency, distinctive personality, calm competence and local expertise</strong> for people who want technology that works without the sales pitch. This living system governs language, visual design and customer journeys across both light and dark themes.
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 01. Brand Positioning -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-line">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-accent-ink">01. Brand Positioning</h2>

            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-12">
                <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line text-center">
                    <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent/20 text-accent-ink mx-auto mb-4" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"></path></svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-2">Transparent</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">No hardware markups. No hidden call-out fees. What you see is what you pay. Pricing is stripped down to the service and the hardware — shown separately.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line text-center">
                    <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent/20 text-accent-ink mx-auto mb-4" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3.055 11H5a2 2 0 012 2v1a2 2 0 002 2 2 2 0 012 2v2.945M8 3.935V5.5A2.5 2.5 0 0010.5 8h.5a2 2 0 012 2 2 2 0 104 0 2 2 0 012-2h1.064M15 20.488V18a2 2 0 012-2h3.064M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-2">Distinctive</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">We use cheeky confidence to be memorable, then support it with plain-English scope, calm competence and practical next steps.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line text-center">
                    <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent/20 text-accent-ink mx-auto mb-4" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg class="h-6 w-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17.657 16.657L13.414 20.9a1.998 1.998 0 01-2.827 0l-4.244-4.243a8 8 0 1111.314 0z"></path><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 11a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z"></path></svg>
                    </div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-2">Local</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Ivanhoe and Eaglemont are our patch. We know the streets, the housing stock, and the typical NBN pain points. No call-out fees for either suburb.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 border border-line">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-3">Target Audience</h3>
                <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
                    Homeowners in Ivanhoe (3079) and Eaglemont (3084) who value their time and want technology that works. They are not looking for the cheapest option — they are looking for clarity, competence, and a technician they feel comfortable welcoming into their home. Secondary: renters, home-office workers, and families managing smart devices they did not set up themselves.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 02. Logo & Mark System -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-line">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-accent-ink">02. Logo &amp; Mark System</h2>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-12">
                <!-- Graphic Mark -->
                <div class="p-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface border border-line">
                    <svg class="h-28 w-auto text-ink" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                        <rect x="15" y="10" width="25" height="80" fill="currentColor"/>
                        <path d="M40 10 L65 90 H90 V10 H65 V90" stroke="#FF8C69" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-linecap="square"/>
                    </svg>
                    <div class="text-center">
                        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink/60">Graphic Mark</p>
                        <p class="text-xs mt-2 leading-relaxed text-ink/50">Rectangle + angular path</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Wordmark -->
                <div class="p-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface border border-line md:col-span-2 overflow-hidden">
                    <span class="text-6xl md:text-7xl font-extrabold text-ink tracking-tight whitespace-nowrap">NAKED TECH</span>
                    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink/60">Wordmark — Inter Extra Bold, tracking-tight</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Horizontal Lockup -->
                <div class="p-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface border border-line md:col-span-2 overflow-hidden">
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                        <svg class="h-10 w-auto text-ink" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                            <rect x="15" y="10" width="25" height="80" fill="currentColor"/>
                            <path d="M40 10 L65 90 H90 V10 H65 V90" stroke="#FF8C69" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-linecap="square"/>
                        </svg>
                        <span class="text-xl font-bold tracking-wide text-ink">NAKED TECH</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink/60">Horizontal Lockup (Header Default)</p>
                </div>

                <!-- Stacked Lockup -->
                <div class="p-10 flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 rounded-2xl bg-inverse border border-white/10">
                    <svg class="h-16 w-auto" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                        <rect x="15" y="10" width="25" height="80" fill="#F7F4EF"/>
                        <path d="M40 10 L65 90 H90 V10 H65 V90" stroke="#FF8C69" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="miter" stroke-linecap="square"/>
                    </svg>
                    <span class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-inverse-ink">NAKED TECH</span>
                    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-inverse-ink/50">Stacked Lockup (Dark Surfaces)</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Clearspace & Minimum Size -->
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
                <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-4">Clearspace</h3>
                    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        Maintain a minimum clearspace equal to the height of the rectangle in the graphic mark (the dark block) on all sides of the logo. No text, graphics, or interface elements should intrude into this zone.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-4">Minimum Size</h3>
                    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed text-sm">
                        The graphic mark should never appear smaller than <strong>40px</strong> tall. The wordmark alone should never appear smaller than <strong>14px</strong> (text-sm equivalent). The horizontal lockup is preferred for most applications at 32–40px mark height.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Misuse -->
            <div class="mt-8 bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-4">Do Not</h3>
                <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm text-ink/70">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink font-bold">✗</span> Stretch, squash, or distort the mark</li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink font-bold">✗</span> Change the mark colors outside the defined palette</li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink font-bold">✗</span> Add drop shadows, gradients, or outlines to the mark</li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink font-bold">✗</span> Rotate the mark or place it on a busy background</li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink font-bold">✗</span> Use the wordmark without the mark as a primary identifier</li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink font-bold">✗</span> Place the mark on a background that reduces contrast (use the dark-surface variant on dark backgrounds)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 03. Color Palette -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-line">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-accent-ink">03. Color Palette</h2>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 mb-8">
                <!-- Skin Bone -->
                <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-line bg-surface">
                    <div class="h-32" style="background-color: #F7F4EF;"></div>
                    <div class="p-4">
                        <p class="font-bold text-sm text-ink">Skin Bone</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 font-mono">#F7F4EF</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 mt-1">Background. Warm off-white. The primary page surface.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Ivanhoe Slate -->
                <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-line bg-surface">
                    <div class="h-32" style="background-color: #2D3035;"></div>
                    <div class="p-4">
                        <p class="font-bold text-sm text-ink">Ivanhoe Slate</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 font-mono">#2D3035</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 mt-1">Text &amp; headings. Dark charcoal with subtle warmth. Hero section backgrounds.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Electric Peach -->
                <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-line bg-surface">
                    <div class="h-32" style="background-color: #FF8C69;"></div>
                    <div class="p-4">
                        <p class="font-bold text-sm text-ink">Electric Peach</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 font-mono">#FF8C69</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 mt-1">Accent. Coral-peach. CTAs, highlights, interactive elements, the path in the logo mark.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Electric Peach Ink -->
                <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-line bg-surface">
                    <div class="h-32" style="background-color: #B84424;"></div>
                    <div class="p-4">
                        <p class="font-bold text-sm text-ink">Peach Ink</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 font-mono">#B84424</p>
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 mt-1">Accessible accent. Terracotta. Accent text and icons on light backgrounds. Meets WCAG AA on skin-bone.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Usage Ratios -->
            <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-4">Usage Ratios</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
                    <strong>Skin Bone</strong> should dominate (~70% of visible surface). <strong>Ivanhoe Slate</strong> is the primary text and dark-section background (~20%). <strong>Electric Peach</strong> is used sparingly (~8%) as the accent — if everything is peach, nothing stands out. <strong>Peach Ink</strong> is used only for accent text on light backgrounds (~2%).
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 04. Typography -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-line">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-accent-ink">04. Typography</h2>

            <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 border border-line space-y-8">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-3">Font Stack</h3>
                    <p class="font-mono text-sm text-ink/70 bg-canvas rounded-lg p-4 break-all">
                        'Inter', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-3">Weights</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-4"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest w-16 text-ink/50">400</span><span class="font-normal text-ink">Body text, paragraphs, descriptions</span></div>
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-4"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest w-16 text-ink/50">500</span><span class="font-medium text-ink">Medium emphasis, sub-labels</span></div>
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-4"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest w-16 text-ink/50">600</span><span class="font-semibold text-ink">Navigation, section labels, small headings</span></div>
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-4"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest w-16 text-ink/50">700</span><span class="font-bold text-ink">Card titles, sub-headings, CTAs</span></div>
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-4"><span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest w-16 text-ink/50">800</span><span class="font-extrabold text-ink">Hero headings, h1, key numbers</span></div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-3">Scale</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-3">
                        <p class="text-xs text-ink/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-xs</span> — Fine print, legal footnotes</p>
                        <p class="text-sm text-ink/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-sm</span> — Body captions, card metadata</p>
                        <p class="text-base text-ink/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-base</span> — Primary body, form labels</p>
                        <p class="text-lg text-ink/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-lg</span> — Lead paragraphs, feature descriptions</p>
                        <p class="text-xl text-ink/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-xl</span> — Subtitles, section intros</p>
                        <p class="text-2xl text-ink/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-2xl</span> — Card headings</p>
                        <p class="text-3xl text-ink/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-3xl</span> — Section headings (mobile)</p>
                        <p class="text-4xl text-ink/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-4xl</span> — Section headings (desktop)</p>
                        <p class="text-5xl text-ink/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-5xl</span> — Hero headings (mobile)</p>
                        <p class="text-6xl text-ink/60"><span class="font-mono text-xs">text-6xl</span> — Hero headings (desktop)</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-3">Tracking (Letter Spacing)</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-2 text-sm">
                        <p class="tracking-tight text-ink/70"><span class="font-mono text-xs">tracking-tight</span> — All headings. Pulls the letterforms closer for a tighter, modern feel.</p>
                        <p class="tracking-wide text-ink/70"><span class="font-mono text-xs">tracking-wide</span> — Navigation links, brand wordmark.</p>
                        <p class="tracking-widest text-ink/70"><span class="font-mono text-xs">tracking-widest</span> — Uppercase labels, category tags, section kickers.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 05. Brand Voice -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-line">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-accent-ink">05. Brand Voice</h2>

            <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 border border-line space-y-8">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-3">Tone Principles</h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink/70">
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> <strong>Cheeky but professional.</strong> The brand uses double-entendre and confidence to stand out from the beige IT crowd, but always lands on competence — never crassness.</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> <strong>Transparent about everything.</strong> Pricing, process, hardware costs. If it can be shown, show it. The "naked" metaphor is not just a gag — it is the operating principle.</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> <strong>Confident, not arrogant.</strong> We know what we are doing and say so directly. We do not overpromise or pretend problems do not exist.</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> <strong>Local, not generic.</strong> References to Ivanhoe, Eaglemont, 3079 and 3084 — these are not SEO keywords. They are the actual places we serve and the actual people we talk to.</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> <strong>Context determines tone.</strong> Routine technology can be playful. Scam, security, loss and urgent situations require calm, factual, non-judgemental language.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-3">The "Naked" Metaphor — Rules of Engagement</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-ink/70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                        The brand name is a double-entendre. It works because it is both descriptive (naked = transparent, nothing hidden) and playful. The line is: <strong>playful, never sleazy.</strong>
                    </p>
                    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                        <div class="bg-surface-muted rounded-xl p-5 border border-line">
                            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-bold text-accent-ink mb-2">Do ✓</p>
                            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-ink/80">
                                <li>"We turn things on."</li>
                                <li>"Total transparency. Our clothes-off policy."</li>
                                <li>"We handle your hardware with care."</li>
                                <li>"Lock it in."</li>
                                <li>"Secure your slot."</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="bg-urgent-surface rounded-xl p-5 border border-accent/30">
                            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-bold text-accent-ink mb-2">Don't ✗</p>
                            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-ink/80">
                                <li>Anything that implies sexual availability of staff</li>
                                <li>Jokes about "happy endings" or "extras"</li>
                                <li>Objectifying language about technicians' bodies</li>
                                <li>"We'll make your hardware happy" (too far)</li>
                                <li>Any reference to clients undressing</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-3">Voice Spectrum</h3>
                    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-surface-muted p-5">
                            <p class="font-bold">Playful</p>
                            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Brand moments, routine setup and everyday frustrations. Personality may lead.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-surface-muted p-5">
                            <p class="font-bold">Practical</p>
                            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Pricing, process and technical choices. Clarity leads; humour is restrained.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="rounded-xl bg-urgent-surface p-5">
                            <p class="font-bold">Calm</p>
                            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Scams, security, money or loss. Safety and non-judgemental guidance lead; jokes stop.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 06. Imagery -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-line">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-accent-ink">06. Imagery</h2>

            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
                <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-4">Photo Direction</h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink/70">
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> Sun-drenched, warm, natural light — Australian residential interiors</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> Technician-forward: the person is the subject, not the hardware</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> Locations should feel like real Ivanhoe homes — not sterile showrooms</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> Avoid: stock-photo "IT guy in server room" tropes</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line">
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-4">Treatment</h3>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink/70">
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> Slight warmth boost — pull the temperature toward the peach/gold range</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> Natural contrast — avoid heavy HDR or over-sharpening</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> No heavy filters, no monochrome, no desaturation</li>
                        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-accent-ink">▪</span> Hero images: 16:9 or similar landscape ratio, WebP format, optimized for 2x displays</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 07. Components -->
        <section class="mb-16 pt-16 border-t border-line">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-accent-ink">07. Components</h2>

            <!-- CTA Button -->
            <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-4">Primary CTA Button</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink/70 mb-6">The rounded-full electric-peach button is the primary action element. Used in the header, hero sections, and bottom-of-page CTAs.</p>
                <div class="bg-canvas rounded-xl p-8 flex justify-center">
                    <span class="inline-flex min-h-14 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent px-10 py-4 text-lg font-bold text-ivanhoe-slate shadow-xl shadow-electric-peach/30 cursor-default">
                        BOOK A VISIT
                    </span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-xs font-mono text-ink/40 mt-4 text-center">rounded-full bg-accent shadow-lg shadow-electric-peach/30 hover:scale-105 hover:bg-[#FF7A50]</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Dark Section -->
            <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-4">Dark Section</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink/70 mb-6">Used for hero headers and high-contrast content blocks. Ivanhoe Slate background with Skin Bone text, Electric Peach accents.</p>
                <div class="bg-inverse rounded-xl p-10 text-center">
                    <h4 class="text-3xl font-bold text-inverse-ink mb-2">Total Transparency.</h4>
                    <p class="text-inverse-ink/70">We believe in showing you everything.</p>
                    <div class="w-16 h-1 bg-accent mx-auto mt-4"></div>
                </div>
                <p class="text-xs font-mono text-ink/40 mt-4 text-center">bg-inverse text-inverse-ink + electric-peach accent bar</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Service Card -->
            <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line mb-8">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-4">Service Card</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink/70 mb-6">White rounded-2xl cards with subtle border, icon circle, category label, title, description, and text link. Subtle hover lift.</p>
                <div class="bg-canvas rounded-xl p-8 flex justify-center">
                    <article class="flex h-full flex-col rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-6 shadow-sm transition hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-xl w-72 cursor-default">
                        <div class="mb-4 flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-canvas text-accent" aria-hidden="true">
                            <svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"></path></svg>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-ink">Category Label</p>
                        <h4 class="mt-2 text-lg font-bold text-ink">Service Name</h4>
                        <p class="mt-2 flex-grow text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">Short card description explaining the service in one sentence.</p>
                        <span class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-sm font-bold text-ink hover:text-accent">Learn more <span class="ml-2" aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Structured Footer -->
            <div class="bg-surface rounded-2xl p-8 border border-line">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink mb-4">Structured Footer</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink/70 mb-6">The footer is the final routing surface: brand and contact first, then problem help, project services and company information. Corporate attribution and theme controls sit in the utility bar.</p>
                <div class="bg-inverse rounded-xl p-6 text-inverse-ink">
                    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">Help with a problem</p>
                    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 text-sm text-inverse-ink/70 sm:grid-cols-3">
                        <span>Wi-Fi keeps dropping</span>
                        <span>Computer running slowly</span>
                        <span>Scam or account concern</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 08. Theme System -->
        <section class="mb-24 pt-16 border-t border-line">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-accent-ink">08. Light &amp; Dark Theme System</h2>
            <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
                <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#DDD8D1] bg-[#F7F4EF] p-8 text-[#2D3035] shadow-sm">
                    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[#B84424]">Light theme</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-extrabold">Warm and open.</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[#606369]">Skin Bone canvas, white elevated surfaces and Ivanhoe Slate text create a domestic, approachable default.</p>
                    <span class="mt-6 inline-flex rounded-full bg-[#FF8C69] px-5 py-3 font-bold text-[#2D3035]">Primary action</span>
                </div>
                <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#43464B] bg-[#141619] p-8 text-[#F7F4EF] shadow-sm">
                    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[#FFA68B]">Dark theme</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-extrabold">Warm, not cyberpunk.</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[#BEBAB4]">Deep charcoal replaces pure black, with warm bone text and restrained peach accents preserving the residential character.</p>
                    <span class="mt-6 inline-flex rounded-full bg-[#FF8C69] px-5 py-3 font-bold text-[#2D3035]">Primary action</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr]">
                <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-8">
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Semantic colour roles</h3>
                    <dl class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
                        <div><dt class="font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink">canvas</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink/70">Primary page background</dd></div>
                        <div><dt class="font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink">surface</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink/70">Cards, menus and elevated panels</dd></div>
                        <div><dt class="font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink">ink / muted</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink/70">Primary and secondary copy</dd></div>
                        <div><dt class="font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink">line</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink/70">Borders and separation</dd></div>
                        <div><dt class="font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink">inverse</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink/70">High-contrast sections and footer</dd></div>
                        <div><dt class="font-mono text-xs text-accent-ink">accent / accent-ink</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink/70">Actions and accessible emphasis</dd></div>
                    </dl>
                </div>
                <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-8">
                    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Behaviour</h3>
                    <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink/70">
                        <li>Follow the operating-system preference on first visit.</li>
                        <li>Offer System, Light and Dark controls in navigation and footer.</li>
                        <li>Persist an explicit user choice without a theme flash.</li>
                        <li>Update browser chrome and embedded content colour scheme.</li>
                        <li>Never use theme changes to reduce contrast or hide focus states.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 09. Experience Principles -->
        <section class="mb-16 pt-16 border-t border-line">
            <h2 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold mb-12 text-accent-ink">09. Experience Principles</h2>
            <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
                <article class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-8">
                    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-ink">Problem first</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold">Use the customer’s language.</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Lead with “Wi-Fi keeps dropping” or “My computer is slow,” then introduce the assessment and branded service name. Internal categories never outrank the visitor’s problem.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-8">
                    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-ink">Contextual navigation</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold">Keep people where the answer is.</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Global navigation may adapt its destination to the page. “How it works” targets the local process on service pages and the overview on the homepage.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-8">
                    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-ink">Progressive detail</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold">Route first. Explain second.</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/70">The homepage helps visitors choose a path. Service hubs compare offers. Landing pages carry the detailed scope, exclusions and decision support.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-8">
                    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent-ink">Accessible restraint</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold">Motion and personality never block the task.</h3>
                    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/70">Maintain keyboard access, visible focus, 44px minimum targets, reduced-motion support and readable contrast in both themes.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

    </div>
</div>
